:56', 'title': 'ExxonMobil Reports Q1 Loss Of $0.14 Per Share', 'text': "REPORTS RESULTS FOR FIRST QUARTER 2020.Q1 LOSS PER SHARE $0.14.SAYS REDUCING 2020 CAPITAL AND OPERATING SPEND TO MANAGE UNPRECEDENTED MARKET CHALLENGES.Q1 LOSS OF $610 MILLION DRIVEN BY $2.9 BILLION NONCASH CHARGE FROM MARKET-RELATED WRITE-DOWNS.QUARTERLY OIL‑EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION WAS 4 MILLION BARRELS PER DAY, UP 2 PERCENT FROM Q1 OF 2019.SAYS CAPEX IS NOW EXPECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY $23 BILLION FOR YEAR, DOWN FROM PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED GUIDANCE OF $33 BILLION..SAYS EXCLUDING ENTITLEMENT EFFECTS AND DIVESTMENTS, QUARTERLY OIL‑EQUIVALENT PRODUCTION WAS UP 5 PERCENT FROM PRIOR YEAR.QUARTERLY LOSS $610 MILLION VERSUS. $2.35 BILLION EARNINGS REPORTED LAST YEAR.SAYS REDUCING 2020 CAPITAL SPENDING BY 30 PERCENT AND CASH OPERATING EXPENSES BY 15 PERCENT.QUARTERLY CAPITAL AND EXPLORATION EXPENDITURES WERE $7.14 BILLION VERSUS $6.89 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.SAYS COVID-19 HAS SIGNIFICANTLY IMPACTED NEAR-TERM DEMAND, RESULTING IN OVERSUPPLIED MARKETS, UNPRECEDENTED PRESSURE ON COMMODITY PRICES, MARGINS.SAYS EXXONMOBIL'S CAPITAL ALLOCATION PRIORITIES REMAIN UNCHANGED.QUARTERLY UPSTREAM EARNINGS WERE $536 MILLION VERSUS $2.88 BILLION REPORTED LAST YEAR.QUARTERLY RESULTS INCLUDED A $2.9 BILLION CHARGE FROM IDENTIFIED ITEMS, OR $0.67 PER SHARE ASSUMING DILUTION.QUARTERLY WORLDWIDE REFINERY THROUGHPUT 4,060 KBD VERSUS. 3,886 KBD REPORTED LAST YEAR."}{'symbol': 'FB', 'date': '2020-05-01 14:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Facebook Warned That It May Lose A Key Seal Of Approval For Ad Measurement - WSJ', 'text': ':FACEBOOK WARNED THAT IT MAY LOSE A KEY SEAL OF APPROVAL FOR AD MEASUREMENT'}{'symbol': 'GILD', 'date': '2020-05-01 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Gilead Sciences Reports First Quarter 2020 Financial Results', 'text': "GILEAD SCIENCES ANNOUNCES FIRST QUARTER 2020 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q1 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.68.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.22.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.57 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.TOTAL REV